# game1-server: what the program may do (docs/PERMISSIONS.md).  Without this file an app may do
# everything; with it, everything that is not listed is refused (in the library, plugins,
# scripts and agent actions too).  The app's own folders (config://, data://, cache://,
# logs://) and app:// need no line.  The build checks the syntax; the packages follow the file
# (Flatpak finish-args, MSIX capabilities: docs/PACKAGING.md).
# the server: UDP and the WebSocket on the address of --bind (127.0.0.1 unless set)
net.listen *:*
# the UDP server's answers go to every client's address (plat checks send_to against net.connect: with only
# localhost here a client on the LAN got no CHALLENGE, seen in G7e part 2's first run between two machines);
# --check: a client of its own on the loopback address
net.connect *:*
# --web DIR: the files of the browser build named on the command line
fs.user
